-- title:
--   Non-supersingularity transports along σ on the j-finite chart (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries`$(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb{Q}$; `fieldBar q M'` is the analogous base change of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ (the kernel of a unit-group reduction map); for a field $K$, `modularFunctionFieldC K M'` is the $K$-subfield of `LaurentSeries`$(K)$ generated by `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K M'`; and `ssJSet q Ω` is the set of those $j\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The data are: a prime $q$ together with the hypothesis `hq3 : q = 3`; a non-zero level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`, the predicate `LiesOverPrime`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of those places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w(\,$`jGeomGen`$\,)\in$ `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; the containment `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` in `fieldBar q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility with $A$ and with orders of functions, as in the structure `ConstantReduction`), subject to `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of `Idx q`).
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $=\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$, indexed by $W$. The Igusa-side group of hypotheses consists of: `hIg_inf`, describing $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the point `lineInfty q` $=[1:0]$ as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ non-zero, with $f\cdot x(y)=x(x)$ in the sense that $f$ times the image of $y$ equals the image of $x$ in `LaurentSeries`$(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$; `hIg`, that every point of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ is $\overline{\gamma}\cdot[1:0]$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ (reduction `redQ q`) with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at that point the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\,[1:0]\,)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. The supersingular-side group consists of: `hSS_A`, that for $s\in W$ and $x\in\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ if and only if $x\in A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s\in W$ and $f\in$ `R₀.integers` satisfying $\mathrm{ord}_P(f)\ge 0$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\mathrm{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$ ($j$ being the element with Laurent series `coeffEmb`$\,\bar{\mathbb{Q}}\,$`jq`), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, asserts both that the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that for each $s$ there is $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t$ minus the image of $a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$. Further, a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` with `hR : R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O`, that an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\,[1:0]\,)$.
--
--   The remaining data are arithmetic: an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; a subfield $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with an element $\pi_0$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$, such that the contraction of $A$ to $k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), is Henselian local (`hhens`), has maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`) and algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`); an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0$ of $k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, and an element $\varpi_t$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ which is the contraction of $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a Henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is a statement about intermediate fields of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$, the $k_0$-algebra structure being the one obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with the structure map $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ such that (i) the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`, (ii) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, (iii) for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of $k_0(\text{image of }K')$ with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i (\text{image of }c_i)\,a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$, and (iv) every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose underlying Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb`$\,\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ belongs to $F_0$ — writing $E$ for the join of $k_0(\text{image of }K_1)$ with $F_0$ — the following holds for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $E$ whose structure map sends $a\in A_1$ to the image of $a$ under $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Let $j_1\in E$ be non-zero with image in `fieldBar q M'` the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, included via `hle`, whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb`$\,\bar{\mathbb{Q}}\,$`jq`; write `chartAlgFin A₁ E j₁` for the $A_1$-subalgebra of $E$ of elements integral over $A_1[j_1]$, `XFin A₁ E j₁` for its prime spectrum and `jChartFin A₁ E j₁` for $j_1$ viewed in that subalgebra. Then, for every $j'\in E$ whose underlying Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ equals `coeffEmb`$\,\bar{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\,$`qExpand ℚ q jq`$\,)$ and which lies in `chartAlgFin A₁ E j₁`, for every $A_1$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $E$ with $\sigma j'=j'$ and with $b\in$ `chartAlgFin A₁ E j₁` if and only if $\sigma b\in$ `chartAlgFin A₁ E j₁` for all $b\in E$, and for all points $y,y'$ of `XFin A₁ E j₁` such that for every $b$ of the chart algebra with $\sigma^{-1}b$ again in the chart algebra one has $b\in y'$ if and only if $\sigma^{-1}b\in y$: if for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A₁ E j₁` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime ideal of $y$ one has $\varphi(\,$`jChartFin A₁ E j₁`$\,)\notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`, then for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi'$ from `chartAlgFin A₁ E j₁` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime ideal of $y'$ one has $\varphi'(\,$`jChartFin A₁ E j₁`$\,)\notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case of the invariance, under an $A_1$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of the level field fixing the $q$-shifted invariant $j(q\tau)$ and preserving the $j$-finite chart algebra, of the property that a point of the chart does not lie over a supersingular $j$-invariant in characteristic $q$; the two points $y$ and $y'$ correspond under $\sigma$. It is used in the construction of a level automorphism centring the two-chart integral model away from the supersingular tubes, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube_of_eq_three).
